! 225020.00 (a half word; next 225020.40).  Remarks run -0751 .. -0787
! (decimal; none printed on lines 7, 15, 20, 23-25, 31-38, 43-45, 48,
! 51, 53; -0764, -0769, -0772 are never printed).
!
! GLYPHS SETTLED BY SOMETHING OTHER THAN PLAIN INK:
!  * line 32 ",DICCEF" is DIODEF: binary 000015.00 = 13.0 = p.105's
!    DIODEF SYN,13.0 (O and D both worn to C).
!  * line 36 ",DCCMM" is DCOMM: binary 000043.40 = 35.32 = p.105 DCOMM.
!  * line 39 "B,V RTIC1" is VRTIO1: p.221's label at 224422.00, and the
!    binary prints 224422.10.
!  * line 40's label prints "V CNLIN"; the first glyph has a straight
!    left stem.  Written VONLIN: p.215 line 4 prints B,V ONLIN ->
!    225010.50, this label's address.
!  * line 41 "V TSB+V CS" is V DS: VDS from line 14 (3.40) + VTSB =
!    225224.40, the printed SV address .51 - J(4)*2 - 1.
!  * lines 43/44 print ZCOM9? / ZASN?1 with a round glyph that ink
!    alone does not settle as O or 0.  Written ZCOM90 and ZASN01: the
!    defining page (vol 2 printed p.297, not landed) reads "Z COM 90" at
!    232762.00 and "ASN 01" at 232746.00, in the numbered families ZASN06
!    /50/52/99 and ZCOM95/98.
!  * octal-field opens ("C00006.62", "001000.CC") are 0; hex bytes
!    printed with an open round are 0 where the statement makes 0
!    (lines 10/16/44/52 "C0" -> 00 or C0 per assembly, see !CHECKs).
!
